//RS //! D-JPK-CACHE1=A (U24) — the A4 hangar-object envelope.
//RS //!
//RS //! Every realized hangar object carries a small identity block that makes it a
//RS //! cache-substitutable artifact: the content hash of its output tree, the
//RS //! platform it was built for, a detached-signature slot (filled by package
//RS //! signing, card #13), and provenance (how it was produced). These fields are
//RS //! frozen into the hangar/lock schema now — the binary-cache protocol that
//RS //! consumes them is a later card (D-JPK-CACHE1 protocol slice). A
//RS //! build-from-source output is an envelope-carrying object exactly like a
//RS //! substituted one, so the resolver never has to care which path produced it.
//RS //!
//RS //! E4-JP1 Hangar Store v2: the canonical archive digests uncompressed logical
//RS //! bytes (sparse holes hash as zero-filled logical content; physical allocation
//RS //! is not identity). Path law rejects case-fold collisions, reserved names,
//RS //! trailing-dot/space Windows aliases, and unrepresentable cross-platform
//RS //! names — Unicode normalization is never implicit. Security/quarantine xattrs
//RS //! are excluded from identity; other semantic xattrs require an explicit
//RS //! platform artifact kind or the ingest fails closed.
//RS 
